  "contract": "[6886,68A4) is a fragment of the level-setup routine: LEA FF0690,A5, then BSR 6EC8, 6EDC, 7772, 783A, 7B9C and 7C26, falling through to 68A4. 6EC8 and 6EDC each pop one F9E2 object, store it in FF31B4 / FF31B8 and clear its mode byte, leaving it dormant with F9E2's other defaults (frame 021D, flags 0, 12646/12646 selectors); position, +08..+0D, target, countdown, +1A..+45 and the link are inherited. The twelve pops are ordered; FF31B4, FF31B8 and FF31C0 name members 1, 2 and 10. Native requires verified inherited fields (position and presentation for the dormant members) and zero unrepresented bytes, else rejects with no change. Exhaustion enters the never-returning FA1E loop. Later setup from 68A4, 7AD6 (the only FF31B4/FF31B8 reader) and callback79B6 are not reconstructed."
